From: SinceVIC20 <codedesk@v3biolab.com>
Date: Tue, 27 Oct 2026 08:48:47 -0700
Subject: [PATCH 03/12] firewall: skip loading unused DNS transports in alias
 updates

The alias updater runs every minute and only uses plain DNS, but
importing dnspython loaded its DNS over QUIC and HTTPS support and trio
whenever those packages are installed, as they are by the FreeBSD port.
That took about half of every run, and trio also ran the C compiler and
linker to find a library. Turn those features off before dnspython
loads: a run now takes about 1 s of CPU instead of 2.
---
 src/opnsense/scripts/filter/lib/__init__.py | 5 +++++
 1 file changed, 5 insertions(+)

diff --git a/src/opnsense/scripts/filter/lib/__init__.py b/src/opnsense/scripts/filter/lib/__init__.py
index ffad4727f5..9d6d5585ac 100755
--- a/src/opnsense/scripts/filter/lib/__init__.py
+++ b/src/opnsense/scripts/filter/lib/__init__.py
@@ -24,6 +24,11 @@
     POSSIBILITY OF SUCH DAMAGE.
 """
 import asyncio
+import dns._features
+# Plain DNS only: skip loading DNS over QUIC/HTTPS and trio, which takes
+# most of the start-up time of every run when those packages are installed.
+for _feature in ('doq', 'doh', 'trio'):
+    dns._features.force(_feature, False)
 import dns.resolver
 import ipaddress
 import itertools
